 :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided context, for the correspondence client configuration in `App/appsettings.json`, the `MaskinportenSettings` object consists of the following three fields:\n- `Authority` [1]\n- `ClientId` [1]\n- `JwkBase64` [1]\n\n**Note on ambiguity/context:** Source [2] documents a different set of Maskinporten settings intended for Altinn CLI (which includes `Environment`, `Scope`, and `EncodedJwk`). However, because your question specifically asks about the correspondence client setup in an app's configuration object, only the three fields listed from Source [1] apply.", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-studio-04-maskinporten-settings-fields", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 324, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "deployed+enrichment", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "lookup,simple,altinn-studio", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "ddda1093665ac R21.9 P2.6 h2.0 or1.7 L7722 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Maskinporten", :response-chars 578, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 7, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "9f86a931737c;1db966514f99", :enrichment-hits 30, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 2, :prompt-tokens 7890, :pool-head "d6052e5e83cfa R22.5 P2.6 h2.0 or1.7 L7818 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Maskinporten ;; d90b62ef8cf4a R22.4 P2.4 h2.0 or0.0 L2648 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Configuration ;; daf9c4ce14a2b R22.4 P3.6 h3.0 or1.4 L2424 1/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | Subscribing ;; d6787cc9ead23 R22.3 P1.4 h1.0 or0.5 L19741 3/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Maskinporten ;; d03002f8d046a R22.0 P2.5 h2.0 or0.7 L2375 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Subscribing ;; d8ac5bf4e1b4b R22.0 P1.4 h1.0 or0.5 L19902 3/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Maskinporten", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "9f86a931737c;1db966514f99", :expected-chunk-ids "1f2453a07f5a", :elapsed-ms 227868, :issued-queries "maskinportensettings appsettings.json | MaskinportenSettings correspondence client App/appsettings.json", :timestamp "2026-06-12T07:57:24.416636Z", :total-tokens 8214, :run-id "8eb2540f-d172-49cb-abe2-103876009ba0", :golden-display-rank 7, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided documentation, you can set the following text/informational properties on an answer alternative (*svaralternativ*) in an Altinn app:\n\n* **`label`** (also referred to as *ledetekst*): This is described as the most common text property and represents the main visible text shown to the user in the UI. It can be provided as plain text or as a language resource key that adapts to the user's selected language [1].\n* **`description`**: Used to provide additional information about an option, supported by `RadioButtons` and `Checkboxes` components [1].\n* **`helpText`**: Provides contextual guidance for the user on those same component types [1].\n\n**Required properties:** \nThe documentation explicitly states that both `label` and `value` are required (*påkrevde egenskaper*) for an option to be valid [1]. While you may freely include or omit `description` and `helpText`, **only `label` is strictly required among the text-related properties** (alongside the mandatory non-text property `value`) [1].\n\nAll these properties can be configured as static values, dynamic expressions, language keys pointing to translation files, or mapped dynamically from a data model structure [1].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? false, :question-id "wg-studio-05-options-text-properties", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 560, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "compound,lookup,altinn-studio,list", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features nil, :response-chars 1202, :source "new", :search-passes 2, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? false, :golden-pool-rank nil, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "458b825c8c3c;97f270fcc1b4", :enrichment-hits 0, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? false, :n-cited 1, :prompt-tokens 7957, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "458b825c8c3c", :expected-chunk-ids "5ed2cd9de2f8", :elapsed-ms 218713, :issued-queries "altinn svaralternativ text property | svaralternatives optionformattext lang defaulttextsrequireddefaulttextid id required formcomponent componenttypes | option formatText lang default_texts_requiredDefault_textId id required | altinn svaralternativ egenskaper property label value description | responseFormat options textResourceBindings", :timestamp "2026-06-12T07:59:08.827858Z", :total-tokens 8517, :run-id "24855049-4058-4d6a-8402-7bdf05f85750", :golden-display-rank nil, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided documentation for Altinn Studio v8, there are two distinct methods for adding options to a component:\n\n**Manual addition (static entries)**  \nYou can add option entries manually by selecting `\"Manuelt\"` and clicking `\"Legg til flere\"` in the settings interface [2]. For each entry, you choose or create custom text that serves as the `label` [2]. Each manual option automatically includes a pre-filled `value`, which is stored when selected [2]. This value defaults to a string but can be changed directly if needed [2]. In your page layout JSON file (`{page}.json`), these are defined inside an `\"options\"` array containing objects with `\"label\"` and `\"value\"` keys, as shown in this example:\n```json{hl_lines=\"4-9\"}\n{\n  \"id\": \"komponent-id\",\n  ...\n  \"options\": [\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Alternativ 1\",\n      \"value\": \"1\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Adding via a source (code list / form data)**  \nAlternatively, you can link the component to a code list based on form data stored within the app itself [1]. Instead of defining static `\"options\"`, you configure a `source` property in your JSON layout file to pull dynamically from existing app data [1]([2]). This approach maps specific fields for how options are grouped and displayed:\n```json{hl_lines=\"4-9\"}\n{\n  \"id\": \"komponent-id\",\n  ...\n  \"source\": {\n    \"group\": \"some.group\",\n    \"label\": \"dropdown.label\",\n    \"value\": \"some.group[].someField\",\n    \"description\": \"\",\n    \"helpText\": \"\"\n  }\n}\n```\nSetting this up requires following specific development instructions for configuring data model sources [1].\n\n**Key difference:** Manual addition stores hardcoded `\"options\"` directly in your layout configuration, giving you full control over each static entry's `label` and `value` [2]. Using a `source` dynamically binds the component to app-formatted code list data, mapping external fields to `group`, `label`, and `value` structures rather than manually typing out every option [1]. Both methods ultimately determine what appears in the UI (`label`) versus what gets stored upon selection (`value`) [1][2].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-studio-06-options-ways-to-add", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 499, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "compound,lookup,altinn-studio,list", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d211bb449d661 R17.4 P2.6 h2.0 or1.0 L7613 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Options page", :response-chars 2080, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 9, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "efd4aa59ddd8;d942c073ba92", :enrichment-hits 0, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 2, :prompt-tokens 7977, :pool-head "dfe65ffe18982 R23.4 P1.4 h1.0 or1.0 L1010 0/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Source ;; d310b6a012fd7 R20.6 P1.5 h1.0 or1.0 L20115 5/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Radiobuttons ;; dc70c4ca52918 R20.6 P1.4 h1.0 or1.0 L15533 0/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Basic form ;; d89b66daad3cd R20.4 P1.4 h1.0 or1.0 L4076 3/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Texts ;; dedd0cd02cacb R20.1 P2.5 h2.0 or1.0 L28909 4/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Multipleselect ;; d7c7ea3cac3fd R19.9 P1.5 h1.0 or1.0 L28847 5/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Dropdown ;; d951d10f46ae9 R18.6 P1.5 h1.0 or1.0 L28915 4/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Checkboxes ;; d434c9d990623 R17.9 P1.4 h1.0 or1.0 L11884 1/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Subform", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "efd4aa59ddd8;d942c073ba92", :expected-chunk-ids "71fd50fc407f", :elapsed-ms 200297, :issued-queries "how to add options component altinn studio | optioner kodeverk optionsett kodlister | legg til valgkomponenter alternativkoder", :timestamp "2026-06-12T08:00:44.715816Z", :total-tokens 8476, :run-id "4dcd56bc-4016-4ebc-8274-33608fb66e47", :golden-display-rank 9, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided documentation, there are three distinct ways (configuration properties) to add options to an options-enabled component in Altinn Studio [2]. Each method serves a different use case and maps directly to how you want to manage your option data:\n\n**1. Manually defined static options (`options`)**\nYou can define options directly within the component's configuration without linking to external lists [1]. In the Altinn Studio Designer, this is done by selecting \"Manuelt\" and clicking \"Legg til flere\", where you manually assign a `label` for each option and optionally edit the pre-filled `value` string that gets submitted when selected [1][2]. The underlying JSON structure uses an `\"options\"` array containing objects with `\"label\"` and `\"value\"` keys, making this method best for small, static lists defined per-component [1][3].\n\n**2. Code lists (`optionsId`)**\nInstead of manually typing options, you can link the component to a predefined list by setting the `optionsId` property in your configuration [1]. This points the component to either code lists stored in JSON files, dynamic code lists, or shared/common code lists (such as standard national registers for countries, counties, municipalities, etc.) that do not require manual maintenance within your app [2][4]. In the Designer interface, you select \"Kodeliste\", enter the specific list ID, and can optionally enable `\"secure\": true` if working with secured dynamic code lists [1][3].\n\n**3. Data model sources (`source`)**\nA third method involves linking the component to options stored as form data within your application itself by using the `source` property [1][3]. This pulls option labels and values directly from repeating structures in your app's data model rather than static files or shared registries [2]. The configuration requires mapping `\"group\"`, `\"label\"`, and `\"value\"` to specific JSON paths that exist inside your running application's form data (e.g., pointing `value` to a path like `\"some.group[].someField\"`) [1][3].\n\n**Important note on precedence:**\nIf you configure more than one of these properties, Altinn Studio applies a strict fallback order: the configuration will ignore lower-precedence settings in favor of higher ones. Specifically, `source` takes precedence over `optionsId`, which takes precedence over `options` [2]. At least one property must be defined for an options-enabled component to function correctly [2].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-studio-06-options-ways-to-add", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 537, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed+enrichment", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "compound,lookup,altinn-studio,list", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d211bb449d661 R18.6 P1.5 h1.0 or0.8 L7613 0/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Options page", :response-chars 2441, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 4, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "71fd50fc407f;3d189734f3ac;efd4aa59ddd8;5ecd5b14b54d", :enrichment-hits 65, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 4, :prompt-tokens 7897, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "71fd50fc407f;3d189734f3ac;efd4aa59ddd8;5ecd5b14b54d", :expected-chunk-ids "71fd50fc407f", :elapsed-ms 279578, :issued-queries "options component Altinn Studio legge til valg manuell kodekiste kodelister | tilgjengelige_verdier code list options dropdown choice | manuelle alternativer valgte verdier komponent_altinn_studio", :timestamp "2026-06-12T08:03:48.407963Z", :total-tokens 8434, :run-id "0fe90eb1-b039-494e-81da-86e24efee362", :golden-display-rank 1, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0} {:response "Based on the provided context, here are all the top-level properties defined in `template.json` along with their data types and requirement status [1]:\n\n**Required Properties:**\n* `schemaVersion` (string): Indicates which JSON Schema version the template follows. Currently, only `\"0.1\"` is supported.\n* `id` (string): Unique ID for the template.\n* `owner` (string): Owner of the template (organization short name).\n* `name` (string): Name of the template.\n* `description` (string): Description of the template.\n\n**Optional Properties:**\n* `remove` (array): List of relative file paths or globs to remove from the application repository when applied [1].\n* `packageReferences` (array): Specifies NuGet packages to add to or update in specified `.csproj` project files [1]. Each array item must contain a `project`, `include`, and `version` property, with no absolute paths allowed for the `project` field [1].\n* `nextSteps` (array): Provides guidance for users on required configuration, code changes, or documentation steps after applying the template [2]. This step requires a `title` (min. 5 chars) and `description` (min. 20 chars), with optional `type` (`configuration`, `codechange`, or `documentation`) and `links` arrays [2].\n\nAll required fields are marked as `\"Yes\"` in the source table, while all other listed properties accept a value of `\"No\"` for the Required column [1].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-studio-07-custom-template-fields", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 369, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "compound,lookup,altinn-studio,list", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d2a699d13cf93 R22.7 P2.6 h2.0 or1.3 L7149 2/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Custom templates", :response-chars 1385, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1,