 :timestamp "2026-06-12T12:25:41.747788Z", :total-tokens 103476, :run-id "22892618-20a3-49cd-ba38-c394dbf46c9e", :golden-display-rank 2, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided documentation, transferring a file using the Altinn 2 Broker SOAP transition interface consists of three explicit steps [2]:\n\n1. **Initiate file transfer**: Call the `InitiateBrokerServiceBasic` endpoint to start the transaction and obtain a reference ID for the upload session [2].\n2. **Upload File**: Use the `StreamedPayloadBasicBE` function within the BrokerServiceStreamed endpoint to send the actual file data, providing your system credentials, reportee number, step 1 reference, and filename in the SOAP header [2]. Note that this returns a pseudo-receipt with a ReceiptId of 0 because Altinn 3 processes uploads asynchronously; therefore, the immediate response status will not necessarily reflect the final processing state [1].\n3. **Verify file availability/processing**: As the sender, make a `GetAvailableFilesBasic` request to check for files belonging to the recipient from step 1 [2]. If the upload and subsequent Altinn 3 conversion succeeded, the file will appear in the returned list with a status like \"Uploaded\" or later \"Downloaded\" [2]. (If you need to confirm processing success beyond checking available files, consider implementing REST calls to `Get File Receipt`, though standard receipt endpoints do not contain data for transitioned Altinn 3 services) [1] [3].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-broker-07-soap-transition-steps-en", :empty? false, :llm-calls 2, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 268, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "compound,lookup,list,altinn-broker", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d233774626f6d R21.5 P2.7 h2.0 or0.9 L5930 2/? ty:content+metadata b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.2,0.0] | Soap", :response-chars 1312, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 3, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 10, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "c7a8b41099e9;33f477a9ebce;232ac1471b60", :enrichment-hits 0, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 3, :prompt-tokens 6193, :pool-head "d233774626f6d R23.3 P2.6 h2.0 or1.4 L1518 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Soap ;; db6c43b81c669 R23.3 P2.5 h2.0 or0.8 L385 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Technical overview ;; d83fe140473a6 R22.8 P2.5 h2.0 or0.8 L526 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Usage ;; db6c43b81c669 R22.7 P2.5 h2.0 or0.8 L417 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Technical overview ;; db6c43b81c669 R22.6 P2.5 h2.0 or0.7 L671 3/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Technical overview ;; d233774626f6d R22.4 P2.6 h2.0 or1.3 L2238 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Soap ;; da6f70e374f7c R21.9 P2.5 h2.0 or0.8 L1241 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | About ;; de960d2f402e0 R21.9 P2.5 h2.0 or0.8 L807 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Getting started", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "c7a8b41099e9;33f477a9ebce;232ac1471b60", :expected-chunk-ids "33f477a9ebce", :elapsed-ms 218900, :issued-queries "Altinn 2 Broker SOAP transition interface | file transfer altinn 2 brokering | transfer fil altinn 2 bryggerSOAP", :timestamp "2026-06-12T12:28:59.522740Z", :total-tokens 6461, :run-id "4c161430-c194-45f7-94a3-f8e1edf8c4d8", :golden-display-rank 10, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0} {:response "Based on the provided context, the key technical considerations for using the Altinn 2 to Altinn 3 Broker transition solution are detailed in reference [2], with component naming sourced from [1]. Every claim below is cited immediately after its relevant statement:\n\n**1. Routing & Request Handling via `ServiceCode`/`ServiceEdition`**\nRequests that support specifying `ServiceCode`/`ServiceEdition` values will be instantly identified by Altinn and forwarded to Altinn 3 through the `\"Altinn 3 Broker Transition Service Bridge\"` [2][1]. If these fields exist but remain empty, requests will **not** be transferred at all [2]. For requests where specifying `ServiceCode`/`ServiceEdition` is not possible, the system first performs a lookup in *Altinn 2 Formidling datalager* [2]. Only if no records are found there will the request subsequently be forwarded to Altinn 3 [2].\n\n**2. Authentication & Authorization Flow**\nAuthentication and authorization are primarily executed at the called API endpoint (either Altinn 2 or Altinn 3) [2]. For Altinn 2, these checks occur strictly at the service level before requests are routed through a dedicated endpoint that assumes prior validation is correct; within Altinn 3, all authentication/authorization occurs internally in its own environment [2]. This architecture requires maintaining both an active *Altinn 2 tjeneste* (including corresponding authorization rules and SRR configuration) **and** an *Altinn 3 Broker Resource* with permissions explicitly defined in the Ressursregisteret [2] while noting that this pattern is standard for transitioning existing services but warrants caution when provisioning dedicated test environments.\n\n**3. File Size Constraints (`MaxFileSize`)**\nFiles transferred through this solution cannot exceed **1 GB**, as this reflects the absolute maximum file size historically enforced by Altinn 2 and applies uniformly across both platforms; any service configured within the transition framework must be explicitly set with a `MaxFileSize` constraint matching this boundary [2].\n\n**4. Storage Location & Cross-Platform Availability**\nFile data and metadata are stored exclusively in *Altinn 3 datalager*, while Altinn 2 Formidlingstjeneste calls themselves are routed over to the Altinn 3 environment; transferred folders/objects remain simultaneously accessible for both Altinn 2 and Altinn 3 users [2].\n\n**5. Receipts (`Kvitteringer`) Behavior Shift**\nTraditional receipts will no longer be persisted in the Altinn 2 system after transition is active, as a pseudo-receipt replaces it by being generated directly from metadata residing in *Altinn 3* instead; consequently, the legacy confirmation service (*kvitteringstjeneste*) inside Altinn 2 stops functioning for forwarded services and requires users to submit an explicit functional request if receipt handling remains mandatory during forwarding operations [2].\n\n**6. Manifest File (`Manifestfil`) Support Status**\nOut-of-the-box usage of manifest files in submitted file data is no longer supported natively within the transition solution; however, this capability can be manually enabled/activated through specific configuration toggles (detailed steps are documented separately) [2].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-broker-06-transition-considerations-en", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 527, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "deployed+enrichment", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "lookup,list,altinn-broker,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "db6c43b81c669 R21.2 P3.6 h3.0 or0.8 L2528 2/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.1,0.0] +q | Technical overview", :response-chars 3225, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 4, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 9, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "63c3d3e28820;c48747e2b5eb;3815339142c4;ac4f2dd7a303", :enrichment-hits 49, :n-expected 1, :stat