notifications.create` [1]. Digdir delegates this scope to registered service owners, who can register new Maskinporten integrations and view their assigned scopes in Samarbeidsportalen [1]. The provided context does not describe any other forms of authentication or authorization.", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-notif-07-api-auth-types", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 0.0, :completion-tokens 451, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 0.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "compound,lookup,altinn-notifications,list", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d56e5162b31f1 R24.7 P2.7 h2.0 or1.6 L3540 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Api", :response-chars 514, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 2, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 13, :golden-read? false, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? false, :retrieved-chunk-ids "0b1c809914f4;5e6a1413b386", :enrichment-hits 0, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 0.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 1, :prompt-tokens 7502, :pool-head "d56e5162b31f1 R28.2 P2.7 h2.0 or1.6 L433 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Api ;; d18f6f9574ff7 R27.9 P2.6 h2.0 or1.5 L626 2/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | About ;; dc04812cefb62 R26.2 P2.6 h2.0 or1.5 L742 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | What do you get ;; dc04812cefb62 R26.0 P2.6 h2.0 or1.5 L558 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | What do you get ;; d18f6f9574ff7 R25.9 P1.4 h1.0 or1.0 L802 0/? ty:content b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | About ;; d6d6d14f8b521 R25.5 P2.7 h2.0 or1.5 L798 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Altinn service ;; d21c46d54d2a2 R25.4 P2.7 h2.0 or1.5 L869 0/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Instant notifications ;; dce838151ccd5 R25.4 P2.6 h2.0 or1.5 L1475 1/? ty:content+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] | Instant notifications", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "0b1c809914f4", :expected-chunk-ids "48ff4cb13723", :elapsed-ms 238430, :issued-queries "altinn notifications api | notificationer auth | notifications autentisering autorisasjon", :timestamp "2026-06-12T13:16:16.950976Z", :total-tokens 7953, :run-id "c7ea7139-2c70-42d5-b0a2-63ed7a0075b7", :golden-display-rank 13, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 0.0} {:response "Based on the provided documentation, the Altinn Notifications API describes three distinct forms of authentication and authorization:\n\n- **Altinn token**: This is the primary authentication method, secured using OAuth2 [1]. Every request must include a valid token either in the `Authorization` header or within the `_AltinnStudioRuntime_ cookie` [1]. External systems typically obtain this by generating a Maskinporten or ID-Porten token and exchanging it for an Altinn token before calling the API [1].\n- **Maskinporten scopes**: Some specific endpoints require additional authorization beyond the base token, specifically through a `Maskinporten scope`, which acts as a permission linked to your integration instance that issues tokens upon request [1].\n- **Platform Access token**: A subset of the API's endpoints is restricted exclusively to callers operating within the Altinn ecosystem and requires this specific token for access [1]. The documentation defers generation instructions to each client system's own developer documentation rather than detailing a unified exchange process here [1].\n\nThe source material treats these as separate authorization layers depending on the endpoint scope and caller environment, without merging them into a single mechanism. All information is sourced from `[1]`.", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "wg-notif-07-api-auth-types", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :ci